# which keys are lit: the same rule an editor asks before acting, so a lit key acts and a dim one does not. While a node is dragged only free-hand and the window keys; while auditioning only the mouse editing dims. b's action is what it WOULD do -- worked out here by doing it on a copy, in the C++ by predicting
