# dragging a dot: a gap between dots is a quarter of the map, in steps of 0.01, stopping 0.01 short of a neighbour; and which dot a click is on
EDIT levels_drag ANALYTIC
GRID FREE
DO example
EXPECT 1 0 ""
STATE N O@0.3,0.5 N@0.3,0.8 E@0.5,0.5 S@0.3,0.2 W@0.1,0.5 A@0.65,0.35 B@0.9,0.35 C@0.9,0.65 D@0.65,0.65 | R O,N,E O,E,S O,S,W O,W,N A,B,C,D | O front:0:1 left:1:1 right:2:1 rear:3:1 | L O>front:1 O>left:1 O>right:1 O>rear:1 N>front:1 E>right:1 S>rear:1 W>left:1 B>right:1 B>~:1 C>left:1 C>right:1 D>rear:1 D>~:0.333333 | D sub:4:N,O | C front | S front | A 1
DO newlevel 1
EXPECT 1 0 "new level 2 of 2, at 0.25, with 9 outputs of its own"
STATE N O@0.3,0.5 N@0.3,0.8 E@0.5,0.5 S@0.3,0.2 W@0.1,0.5 A@0.65,0.35 B@0.9,0.35 C@0.9,0.65 D@0.65,0.65 | R O,N,E O,E,S O,S,W O,W,N A,B,C,D | O front:0:1 left:1:1 right:2:1 rear:3:1 O-2:5:1 N-2:6:1 E-2:7:1 S-2:8:1 W-2:9:1 A-2:10:1 B-2:11:1 C-2:12:1 D-2:13:1 | L O>O-2:4 N>N-2:1 E>E-2:1 S>S-2:1 W>W-2:1 A>A-2:1 B>B-2:1 B>~:1 C>C-2:2 D>D-2:1 D>~:0.333333 | D sub:4:N,O | C front | S front | A 1 | V 1 | Z0 0 K O>front:1 O>left:1 O>right:1 O>rear:1 N>front:1 E>right:1 S>rear:1 W>left:1 B>right:1 B>~:1 C>left:1 C>right:1 D>rear:1 D>~:0.333333 | Z1 0.25 K O>O-2:4 N>N-2:1 E>E-2:1 S>S-2:1 W>W-2:1 A>A-2:1 B>B-2:1 B>~:1 C>C-2:2 D>D-2:1 D>~:0.333333
DO newlevel 1
EXPECT 1 0 "new level 3 of 3, at 0.5, with 9 outputs of its own"
STATE N O@0.3,0.5 N@0.3,0.8 E@0.5,0.5 S@0.3,0.2 W@0.1,0.5 A@0.65,0.35 B@0.9,0.35 C@0.9,0.65 D@0.65,0.65 | R O,N,E O,E,S O,S,W O,W,N A,B,C,D | O front:0:1 left:1:1 right:2:1 rear:3:1 O-2:5:1 N-2:6:1 E-2:7:1 S-2:8:1 W-2:9:1 A-2:10:1 B-2:11:1 C-2:12:1 D-2:13:1 O-3:14:1 N-3:15:1 E-3:16:1 S-3:17:1 W-3:18:1 A-3:19:1 B-3:20:1 C-3:21:1 D-3:22:1 | L O>O-3:4 N>N-3:1 E>E-3:1 S>S-3:1 W>W-3:1 A>A-3:1 B>B-3:1 B>~:1 C>C-3:2 D>D-3:1 D>~:0.333333 | D sub:4:N,O | C front | S front | A 1 | V 2 | Z0 0 K O>front:1 O>left:1 O>right:1 O>rear:1 N>front:1 E>right:1 S>rear:1 W>left:1 B>right:1 B>~:1 C>left:1 C>right:1 D>rear:1 D>~:0.333333 | Z1 0.25 K O>O-2:4 N>N-2:1 E>E-2:1 S>S-2:1 W>W-2:1 A>A-2:1 B>B-2:1 B>~:1 C>C-2:2 D>D-2:1 D>~:0.333333 | Z2 0.5 K O>O-3:4 N>N-3:1 E>E-3:1 S>S-3:1 W>W-3:1 A>A-3:1 B>B-3:1 B>~:1 C>C-3:2 D>D-3:1 D>~:0.333333
SEL only O
DO raise -1 0
EXPECT 1 0 "height -0.05"
STATE N O@0.3,0.5 N@0.3,0.8 E@0.5,0.5 S@0.3,0.2 W@0.1,0.5 A@0.65,0.35 B@0.9,0.35 C@0.9,0.65 D@0.65,0.65 | R O,N,E O,E,S O,S,W O,W,N A,B,C,D | O front:0:1 left:1:1 right:2:1 rear:3:1 O-2:5:1 N-2:6:1 E-2:7:1 S-2:8:1 W-2:9:1 A-2:10:1 B-2:11:1 C-2:12:1 D-2:13:1 O-3:14:1 N-3:15:1 E-3:16:1 S-3:17:1 W-3:18:1 A-3:19:1 B-3:20:1 C-3:21:1 D-3:22:1 | L O>O-3:4 N>N-3:1 E>E-3:1 S>S-3:1 W>W-3:1 A>A-3:1 B>B-3:1 B>~:1 C>C-3:2 D>D-3:1 D>~:0.333333 | D sub:4:N,O | C front | S front | A 1 | V 2 | Z0 0 K O>front:1 O>left:1 O>right:1 O>rear:1 N>front:1 E>right:1 S>rear:1 W>left:1 B>right:1 B>~:1 C>left:1 C>right:1 D>rear:1 D>~:0.333333 | Z1 0.25 K O>O-2:4 N>N-2:1 E>E-2:1 S>S-2:1 W>W-2:1 A>A-2:1 B>B-2:1 B>~:1 C>C-2:2 D>D-2:1 D>~:0.333333 | Z2 0.5 O=0.45 K O>O-3:4 N>N-3:1 E>E-3:1 S>S-3:1 W>W-3:1 A>A-3:1 B>B-3:1 B>~:1 C>C-3:2 D>D-3:1 D>~:0.333333
DRAGLEVEL 1 0 60 EXPECT 0.25
DRAGLEVEL 1 12 60 EXPECT 0.2
DRAGLEVEL 1 -13 60 EXPECT 0.3
DRAGLEVEL 1 200 60 EXPECT 0.01
# up a whole gap: O on the top level is only 0.2 above, so it
# stops at 0.44, 0.01 short
DRAGLEVEL 1 -60 60 EXPECT 0.44
DRAGLEVEL 2 70 60 EXPECT 0.31
DRAGLEVEL 2 -500 60 EXPECT 2.58
DRAGLEVEL 0 40 60 EXPECT -0.17
DOTAT 500 100 10 100 500 EXPECT 0
DOTAT 503 61 10 100 500 EXPECT 1
DOTAT 500 17 10 100 500 EXPECT 2
DOTAT 520 55 10 100 500 EXPECT -1
DOTAT 500 80 10 100 500 EXPECT -1
ENDEDIT

#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROUND 3A-6c: HEIGHTS MATCHED TO THE FIRST NODE, OR FLATTENED
#--------------------------------------------------------------------
# m gives the selected nodes the height, on the current level, of the node selected FIRST; M puts them back at the level's start. All or nothing, refused where a node would reach a level next to it. A box has no first node
