# 3A-9: [ ] set how many rings deep, from the one pointed at
# inward; reaching the centre, it is joined to the centre
# l on the polar grid with a depth: that many rings from the one nearest the point inward, outermost first, joined as four-sided pieces between rings and the innermost ring whole -- or, when they reach it, the centre last, joined to the innermost ring as triangles. Refused past the centre
EDIT layout_rings ANALYTIC
GRID POLAR 0.5 0.5 0.1 8 0
DO layout 0.5 0.8 2 0
EXPECT 1 0 "2 rings, 16 nodes"
